{"total_count":6,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/63418","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/63418/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/63418/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/63418/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/63418","id":3352675847,"node_id":"I_kwDOAQzde87H1cYH","number":63418,"title":"Using PolicySchemeOptions.ForwardDefaultSelector to forward to Microsoft Identity OIDC results in infinite recursion","user":{"login":"deaii","id":134233341,"node_id":"U_kgDOCAA8_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/134233341?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii","html_url":"https://github.com/deaii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deaii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1143445347,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTQzNDQ1MzQ3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-identity","name":"area-identity","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Includes: Identity and providers","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1710398789,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzEwMzk4Nzg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/:heavy_check_mark:%20Resolution:%20Answered","name":":heavy_check_mark: Resolution: Answered","color":"7132ba","default":false,"description":"Resolved because the question asked by the original author has been answered.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1715289215,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzE1Mjg5MjE1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/Status:%20Resolved","name":"Status: Resolved","color":"bbbbbb","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-08-25T17:43:24Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T12:49:04Z","closed_at":"2025-08-29T13:59:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Is there an existing issue for this?\n\n- [x] I have searched the existing issues\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nUsing a custom Policy Scheme with a custom ForwardDefaultSelector that selected between multiple schemes (our service requires different schemes to handle users in different tenants and some legacy scenarios), if the scheme forwards to an OIDC scheme, the service gets locked in an infinite recursion loop, eventually causing an access violation and aborting.\n\nThis uses the latest .NET 8 LTS compatible version of ASP.NET Core and relevant packages.  I've also replicated this behavior when using WSFederation as well as OIDC, but I'm limiting the repro below to OIDC.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nWhen the FowardDefaultSelector returns the name of the scheme matching the OIDC config, the same selector shouldn't be called repeatedly; instead, the rest of the authentication assumes the OIDC scheme rather than the dynamic scheme, and the browser should forward to the Entra OIDC login page.\n\n### Steps To Reproduce\n\n* Clone the repro repo: https://github.com/deaii/fds_repro\n* Replace the Client and Tenant ID in `appsettings.json` with valid entries\n* Put a break point on Program.cs, line 48.\n* Run the project\n* Navigate to https://localhost:<port>/weatherforecast\n* Watch as the Selector function gets called endlessly with an ever-growing stack of recursive goodness.\n\n### Exceptions (if any)\n\nWhen I'm lucky, it's a StackOverflowException.  However, it's usually an access violation that completely overwhelms the console window's history.  I added a breakpoint in the ForwardDefaultSelector and stopped after a few loops and printed the stack below: Note that Authenticationhandler<PolicySchemeOptions>.AuthenticateAsync is called repeatedly:\n\nStack:\n>\tApiProject.dll!Program.<Main>$.__Selector|0_3(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpContext context) Line 48\tC#\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationHandler<System.__Canon>.ResolveTarget(string scheme)\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationHandler<Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.PolicySchemeOptions>.AuthenticateAsync()\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.Core.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationService.AuthenticateAsync(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpContext context, string scheme)\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.RemoteAuthenticationHandler<Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.OpenIdConnect.OpenIdConnectOptions>.HandleAuthenticateAsync()\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationHandler<Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.OpenIdConnect.OpenIdConnectOptions>.AuthenticateAsync()\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.Core.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationService.AuthenticateAsync(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpContext context, string scheme)\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationHandler<Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.PolicySchemeOptions>.AuthenticateAsync()\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.Core.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationService.AuthenticateAsync(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpContext context, string scheme)\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.RemoteAuthenticationHandler<Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.OpenIdConnect.OpenIdConnectOptions>.HandleAuthenticateAsync()\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationHandler<Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.OpenIdConnect.OpenIdConnectOptions>.AuthenticateAsync()\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.Core.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationService.AuthenticateAsync(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpContext context, string scheme)\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationHandler<Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.PolicySchemeOptions>.AuthenticateAsync()\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.Core.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationService.AuthenticateAsync(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpContext context, string scheme)\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.RemoteAuthenticationHandler<Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.OpenIdConnect.OpenIdConnectOptions>.HandleAuthenticateAsync()\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationHandler<Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.OpenIdConnect.OpenIdConnectOptions>.AuthenticateAsync()\tUnknown\n \tMicrosoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.Core.dll!Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationService.AuthenticateAsync(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.HttpContext context, stri